 ### Startup onboarding
 
+Native welcome RPC and account streams reuse the shell-owned cookie from the verified Host launch exchange. They do not depend on a Chromium cookie jar or a Host HTML index. The native HTTP transport binds requests to that Host authority and rejects redirects; no renderer receives its cookie.
+
 The API-key input starts empty and uses `autocomplete="new-password"` to ask Chromium not to autofill saved login passwords.
 
 Repeated launches and `dsh://open` keep the workspace hidden until the startup credential check or a welcome action permits entry. Entering from Welcome places keyboard focus on the document without selecting a sidebar control; Tab navigation remains available.
@@ -281,6 +283,16 @@ Confirmed Host exit without successful task teardown displays localized recovery
 
 <a id="local-desktop-settings"></a>
 
+### Local source updates
+
+Local builds carrying `dshSourceUpdater: true` resolve an explicit `DSH_SOURCE_UPDATER_CONFIG`, then `DSHUpdater/updater-config.json` under the Windows Documents folder, then the legacy `%LOCALAPPDATA%/DSH Source Updater/updater-config.json`. The helper runs under an independent Node executable outside the application installation. Cold and second launches check published official `dsh-v*` releases, including prereleases; concurrent launches share one build and no periodic release polling runs. Reopening also checks again while a previously prepared candidate waits for idle; admission of that candidate pauses until the new check finishes.
+
+The helper builds a fixed release commit with the saved source patch and plugin compatibility checks. An incompatible patch or plugin retains the current installation and opens a warning. The application menu's Source Update Status command displays the current result and offers Retry. An unavailable release service records `check-unavailable` without opening a warning or scheduling retries; the next explicit launch checks again. Check and preparation observers join the same live worker and accept only a completed build matching their pinned target. Missing helper files leave ordinary application startup available.
+
+Installation requires saved drafts, sixty seconds without application input, and no running tasks, approval waits, queued messages or background jobs. Before stopping the Host, a read-only preflight rechecks the candidate, installer, paths and current plugin selection. Missing, added or changed plugins block installation without restoring old plugins. The Host then drains admitted requests and stops gracefully before the helper snapshots the application, Harness home and Electron data. Qualification runs against isolated data with schedules and user admission disabled; matching program and data snapshots remain available for rollback. Packaged mandatory-update policy remains active independently of this local source-update path.
+
+A failed handoff clears the pending switch and stops automatic retries of that candidate. Repeated opens still check for newer published releases; only explicit Retry permits the same rejected candidate again. Repeated identical warnings appear once per application run. Detached installation output is retained in private per-request logs, and acceptance must match the spawned worker PID. A live, unverified helper or failed Host recovery requires local inspection before retrying; the application does not restore a competing Host or quit to authorize an uncertain installation.
+
 ### Local desktop settings
 
 The [shell configuration decision](../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-10-08-desktop-shell-configuration.md) defines Host-independent ownership and the criteria for evaluating existing settings for migration.
